{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
  "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear\nargument next in Case 21-1454, the Ohio\nAdjutant General's Department versus the\nFederal Labor Relations Authority.\nMr. Flowers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLOWERS: Thank you, Mr. Chief\nJustice, and may it please the Court:\nThe Sixth Circuit and the Federal\nLabor Relations Authority held that adjutants\ngeneral and state guards, when they employ\ntechnicians, are federal agencies to which the\nAuthority may issue orders.\nThat is wrong. The Reform Act defines\nagencies to include executive departments,\ngovernment corporations, and independent\nestablishments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FLOWERS",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLOWERS: So let me -- let me try to push back on that. It does make more sense for the Defense Department to be there. For one thing, they control many issues --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FLOWERS",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLOWERS: So the statute delegates to us the power to hire them. I do believe the Defense Department through regulations could say, if you want technicians, you have to agree to collectively bargain on our behalf."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: One, the collective bargaining agreement here is approved by DOD, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Reaves",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners are required to comply with the Act and submit to the FLRA's orders in cases like this one because of the role they play in the federal employment system. It is uncontested that dual-status technicians have collective bargaining rights because they are federal civilian employees who are employed by parts of DOD, a covered agency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Reaves",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. REAVES: The term \"agency\" in the statute includes and requires compliance by components and entities that are designated to act on behalf of that agency, and that includes subcomponents within a federal agency. And that's a thing that Petitioners are most analogous to in this -- in this system that Section 709(d) and Section 709(e) have set forward."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, that -- and I -- that's where I want to pick up. So I'm just curious about the federalism implications of this case. Forget about the militia for the moment, okay? Under the Spending Clause today, the federal government effectively employs or provides the budgets for 30 to 40 percent of state budgets today, and many, many, many of their employees, are they now in other cases, Medicare, Medicaid, the -- the examples that Justice Barrett offered, are they now agents of the federal government effectively? Are they effectively federal agencies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Federation of Labor and Congress of Industrial Organizations",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0003-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the arguments of amici, American Federation of Labor and Congress of Industrial Organizations, they were talking about the National Guards being a unit or a component of DOD."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Ohio says that it would be impractical and even unlawful for it to comply with the collective bargaining order issued in this case and presumably in others as well, and you dispute that. Would you characterize it as an open question on which you have the better of the argument, but there's a risk that Ohio would be right, or do you think Ohio is just crazy to say it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought that the adjutant generals are only subject to the FLRA's authority when they're acting on -- with that hat on, that is, the capacity to be the employer of this group of federal employees. Am I right? Isn't there sort of like really a limited scope of FLRA authority being exerted here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If -- if they're hiring state people or if they're supervising state people, the FLRA is not involved. It's just when this group of federal employees that everybody concedes are there are being supervised by this state officer, must the state officer comply with the Federal Labor Relations Authority about collective bargaining? Am I right about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Grajales (Union Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A ruling in favor of the union here is not going to affect any other aspect of the Petitioners, nor is it going to affect any other state entity. The scheme is completely unique for both technicians but also for the National Guard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Grajales (Union Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the one thing I want to point out is, if bargaining were moved to DOD, it would render parts of the statute inoperative. Under 709(d) and 709(e) and 709(f), the Technicians Act gives day-to-day supervision over working conditions and conditions of employment to the Ohio Adjutant General."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm trying to look at what the -- the Board did below and what the state agency -- Guard, was arguing. Below, I'm not sure why they're collecting the forms that say deduct my union dues, because I thought it was the federal government who paid the dual citizens' salary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "doesn't mention 102, which are the military departments. What do we do about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Flowers (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The quick point responds to Justice Alito's question about the single decision and what do we make of that. This Court in Department of Interior v. FLRA looked at one of those decisions by the Assistant Secretary, and it said, basically, one decision is worth virtually nothing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3568c4a02eddbab839fa6a70a4dbaa93a61d2129a1f6b39396c27985f550813b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3568c4a02edd-0004-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:42 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
